          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A breaker finder and a non-contact voltage tester answer different questions. The finder tells you which breaker to switch off; the tester tells you whether switching it off worked. For any electrical job, you want both answers, and before touching bare wire you want a contact test as well.
          </p>
